  "notes": "The play area's long folding table, bare (white plastic) or under a black cloth to the floor. Reference: docs/SET_DRESSING_REFERENCES.md, 'The walker's trading card shop references (2026-09-15)' -- 'long folding tables (white plastic or covered in a black tablecloth) with black folding chairs, card playmats on the table, piles of cards, deck boxes, dice'. WHAT IS ON IT IS STOCK: `_surface_stock`'s `cards` flavour, planned once per SIDE of the top so two players' worth of dressing face each other. A VARIANT is where the leg frames stand. RANGES: width 1.2 to 3.0 (a 6 ft banquet table is 1.83); depth 0.6 to 0.9; height 0.70 to 0.80. BUDGET: 1,200; measured worst 132 for the table itself plus whatever the stock flavour draws.",
